meta {
  name: Alerts Flow
  seq: 7
}

docs {
  # Alerts Flow - End-to-End Test Suite
  
  Exercises the full alerts lifecycle: infrastructure setup, event emission,
  alert creation referencing a messageId, alert querying, alert event delivery
  to the provider, and immutability enforcement (405 on PUT/DELETE).
  
  ## What This Tests
  
  1. Creates domain/solution/zone infrastructure (solution auto-creates environment-global zone, DEFAULT context, BROKER_SERVICES env, alerts provider)
  2. Creates provider environment with PROVIDE ACL for TESTOBJECT1s, queue, and alerts subscription on environment-global/DEFAULT
  3. Creates consumer environment with SUBSCRIBE ACL, queue, and subscription for TESTOBJECT1s events
  4. Provider emits TESTOBJECT1s event with messageId header (gateway caches context in Redis)
  5. Consumer pulls event off queue and ACKs it
  6. Consumer creates alert referencing the messageId from the event
  7. Verifies alert created with extended elements (sourceEnvironmentId, originatingZoneId, originatingContextId, createdAt)
  8. Lists alerts and verifies collection contains the alert
  9. Gets alert by ID and verifies fields match
  10. Provider pulls alert event off its queue (verifies targeted delivery)
  11. Verifies 405 on PUT and DELETE (alerts are immutable per SIF 3.7)
  
  ## Prerequisites
  
  - All services running (gateway, environment-service, events-connector, queue-service, subscription-service)
  - Admin credentials configured in .env
  
  ## Variable Prefix
  
  All variables use `alt` prefix to avoid conflicts with other test suites.
  
  ## Run Order
  
  Tests are numbered 00-20 and must be run in sequence.
}
